Despite their relevance, very limited research has been
conducted to assess the seasonal cycle and long-term variability of the aerosol mass concentration and chemical composition in the region (Andreae et al., 1995; Annegarn et al.,
1983; Dansie et al., 2017; Eltayeb et al., 1993; Formenti et
al., 1999, 2003b, 2018; Zorn et al., 2008). To fill this gap,
the long-term surface monitoring Henties Bay Aerosol Observatory (HBAO) was established in 2012 on the campus
of the University of Namibia’s Sam Nujoma Marine and
Coastal Resources Research Centre (SANUMARC), along

